Z||000011||FieroRacer||10-22-2001||12:02 AM||||I've done more research into the Nimba Virus.  It's more of a worm that opens a back door for someone to get into a server.  I'm running a fix tool now on my computer which will make sure my system is fully clean.   <A HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/technet/treeview/default.asp?url=/technet/security/topics/Nimda.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.microsoft.com/technet/treeview/default.asp?url=/technet/security/topics/Nimda.asp</A> <BR>For information on Nimba.<BR> <A HREF="http://securityresponse.symantec.com/avcenter/venc/data/w32.nimda.a@mm.removal.tool.html" TARGET=_blank>http://securityresponse.symantec.com/avcenter/venc/data/w32.nimda.a@mm.removal.tool.html</A> <BR>For the tool I'm using.<P>I urge you to have Geocities check all their servers.  I tried looking for a URL to contact them but failed.  Perhaps you have a Tech support E-Mail addy you could use.||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroRacer||10-22-2001||12:31 AM||||I just finished checking my system.  I'm cleaned.  Norton Anti-Virus Did It's Job.  I've found a form that let me at least try contacting Geocities so I tried letting them know their servers are infected.||||reg||6
